This script adds per-column (GC) annotation to an existing input MSA.

If the input MSA has existing RF annotation it will be kept (or rewritten if --rf_cons, --rf_mis or
--rf_x, but gap/nongap column definitions will not be changed).

If the input MSA does not have RF annotation it will be added (unless --rf_no) and RF gap positions
will be defined as positions with > 0.5 fraction gaps (changeable to <x> with --rf_gapthr <x>).

For all added GC annotation, gap RF positions will be gaps ('.'), unless --rf_ignore used in which case
no gaps will appear in added GC annotation.

For all added GC annotation, if --skip is used, positions with > 0.05 gaps (changeable to <x> with
--skip_thr <x>) will be marked as "x" (changeable to <c> with --skip_char <c>).

Per-column annotation descriptions:

CONS:      Most specific IUPAC nt that explains <y> > 0.5 (changeable to <x> with --cons_thr1 <x>)
           if lower case, then <y> < 0.75 (changeable to <y> with --cons_thr2 <y>)
           CONS is always added unless --cons_no is used, or added as RF if --rf_cons is used.

CONSFRACT: <y> value for CONS annotation, encoded as fractional values [0..1] as explained below.
           Only added if --cons_fract used.

INFO:      Information content of each position, only available for DNA or RNA alignments.
           Values range from 0.0 to 2.0 bits and are encoded like fractional values explained below, only
           with values multiplied by 2 (e.g. '*': [1.90..2.00]).

RELENT:    Proxy for relative entropy of each position, with background distribution set as background
           frequency in alignment, across all columns. Actual values range from 0.0 to 1.0, and are calc'ed
           as '1 - e^{-1 * relent}' where relent is the relative entropy (or Kullback-Leibler distance) for
           the given column. The values are encoded as fractional values [0..1] as explained below.

GAPFRACT:  Fraction of seqs that are a gap, encoded as values [0..1] as explained below.
           Only added if --gapfract used.

MIS:       Most-informative-sequence, IUPAC code that corresponds to all nt above background;
           background calculated as the frequency of nt in alignment, across all columns.
           Only added if --mis used. Or added as RF if --rf_mis used.

Encoding of fractional values [0.0..1.0] in CONSFRACT and GAPFRACT annotation:
     '*': [0.95..1.00]
     '9': [0.85..0.95)
     '8': [0.75..0.85)
     '7': [0.65..0.75)
     '6': [0.55..0.65)
     '5': [0.45..0.55)
     '4': [0.35..0.45)
     '3': [0.25..0.35)
     '2': [0.15..0.25)
     '1': [0.05..0.15)
     '0': [0.00..0.05)

